s (fatigue, malaise)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Endocrine Tumor with Cutaneous Manifestations", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.3939393939393939, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The rash's morphology and pain are not typical of paraneoplastic syndromes associated with endocrine tumors, which often present with non-painful, pitting feat…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Adrenal/Endocrine Dysfunction", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.18181818181818188, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Severe hyperglycemia is more specific for insulin resistance or tumors (e.g., glucagonoma) than hypercortisolism. Constitutional symptoms alone are non-specifi…"], "evidence_against": ["Painful, papular/plaque rashes are not typical of adrenal dysfunction (e.g., Cushing's) or pancreatic endocrine tumors. This weakly argues against B2."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.35, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Metabolic Syndrome with Insulin Resistance", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.27272727272727276, "posterior": 0.3636363636363637, "danger": 0.4, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Obesity and smoking are risk factors for insulin resistance, but